    "body": "<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-requirements\">\n<p>You must be a portfolio Owner and also an Owner or Admin in the account(s) that you want to add or remove. </p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HWNHEDGQ0M69V42955Y2XFQS\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to add or remove an account from an existing portfolio in Klaviyo. </p>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>This article is only for those with an existing portfolio. If you do not have a portfolio, see <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/24656917054747\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">how to set up a portfolio</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HWNHEDGQSHP9TYGMR9CPCTX6\">Add an account to a portfolio</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Log in to your portfolio account. </li>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Manage &gt; Accounts</strong>.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28711731645467\" alt=\"Navigation menu for a portfolio account\" width=\"253\" height=\"373\">\n</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Add accounts</strong> in the upper right. </li>\n<li>Check the boxes for the account(s) you want to add.<br>Note: you must be an Owner or Admin in the account you want to add. Any account that you are a user in (but not an Owner or Admin) shows under the <em>Unavailable</em> tab.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28711702669083\" alt=\"Selecting accounts to link to a portfolio\" width=\"624\" height=\"404\">\n</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Add</strong>. </li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HWNHEDGQZT1MP3DTTPYFXDV0\">Remove or delete an account from a portfolio</h2>\n<p>You can remove an account from a portfolio from either the portfolio or through the account directly. </p>\n<h3 id=\"h_01HWNHEDGQR45W6KNV4ZT7V9H0\">Portfolio instructions</h3>\n<p>Only the Owner can remove an account from within the portfolio. To do so:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Log in to your portfolio account. </li>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Manage &gt; Accounts</strong>.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28711731645467\" alt=\"Accounts tab, where you can see every account linked to a portfolio\" width=\"306\" height=\"450\">\n</li>\n<li>Search for the account you want to remove. </li>\n<li>Click the 3-dot menu next to that account. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>Remove from portfolio</strong>.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28711702644635\" alt=\"Menu where you can choose to remove an account from a portfolio\" width=\"624\" height=\"265\">\n</li>\n<li>Confirm by clicking <strong>Remove</strong> in the modal.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28711702649371\" alt=\"Modal to confirm that you want to unlink an account from the portfolio\" width=\"624\" height=\"255\">\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"h_01HWNHEDGQJS57701QJYMYBY9M\">Account instructions</h3>\n<p>From within an account, any Owner or Admin in the account can remove it from a portfolio:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Log in to that account. </li>\n<li>Click the account name on the bottom left.</li>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Settings &gt; Organization</strong>. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Remove from portfolio</strong>.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28711702655643\" alt=\"Organization tab showing the option to unlink the account from a portfolio\" width=\"624\" height=\"217\">\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Remove </strong>in the modal.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28711702662427\" alt=\"Modal to confirm that you want to unlink an account from the portfolio\" width=\"624\" height=\"223\">\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HWNHEDGQQZJS5HDCWV1ZHZAT\">Additional resources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/25185184021019\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How to add or remove a portfolio user</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/25185047957275\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Understanding portfolio reporting</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/25181702319643\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Understanding portfolio user roles</a></li>\n</ul>",
